From aa9547b986bb972b6dba2787411750e216854218 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wunhuang <wunhuang@amd.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 03:28:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: prefill coalescer for DP-attention (faithful ATOM port)

Port ATOM's cross-DP-rank prefill coalescer (ROCm/ATOM#1611) into SGLang's
DP-attention scheduler. Rewrites PrefillDelayer as a tick-based FIRE/HOLD
state machine evaluated every scheduler tick on every DP rank in lockstep via
one cross-DP all_gather, replacing the previous slot/queue-ratio negotiation.

Decision (on the SUM/OR-reduced per-rank state):
  - must-fire bounds: no-decode, KV high/low watermark, end-to-end TTFT queue
    guard (max_queue_ms), single-hold ttft_max_ticks, partial_max_ticks
  - alignment gate: HOLD while any DP rank lacks prefill (anti-skew) so all
    ranks enter prefill together and the MoE collective stays aligned
  - fill target: FIRE once SUM(pending) >= target_fill * (n_prefillable *
    max_prefill_tokens)
  - stall give-up: FIRE if aggregate pending stops growing for stall_ticks

Integrated in Scheduler.get_new_batch_prefill (called every tick before any
early return, preserving lockstep); removes the per-request delayer checks in
PrefillAdder. New server args: --prefill-delayer-target-fill,
--prefill-delayer-max-queue-ms, --prefill-delayer-{ttft,partial,stall}-* ,
--prefill-delayer-kv-high-watermark.

Validated on DeepSeek-V4-Pro (8xMI355X, TBO+DPA dp8, 1k/1k c1024):
  - gsm8k (full 1319): ON 0.939 vs OFF 0.931 -- no accuracy regression
  - throughput A/B (random, request-rate inf):
      uniform  (range-ratio 1.0): ~neutral (prefill already batches full)
      fragmented (range-ratio 0.3): OFF 15,747 -> ON 20,571 tok/s (+30.6%),
        matching ATOM's own coalescer on the same workload (+35.1%)
The gain requires a fragmented / uneven-length DP workload (many small
prefills); uniform simultaneous arrival shows no gain, as expected.

Unit tests rewritten for the new state machine (alignment gate, fill target,
must-fire bounds, stall give-up) in test_prefill_delayer.py.
